===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[board]], having [[letter]]s of the [[alphabet]] and the words [[yes]] and [[no]]; used with a [[planchette]] during a [[seance]] to "[[communicate]]" with [[spirit]]s.
#: {{syn|en|Ouija board|spirit board|talking board}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The use of such a board to attempt to communicate with spirits.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1903|title=The Gentleman from Everywhere|author=James Henry Foss|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/12193/pg12193-images.html|passage=Soon after the departure of my brother to the better land, our spirit-band informed us very plainly through "'''Ouija'''," that it was our duty to remove to Boston in order that our children might have better educational facilities, and be admitted to the "musical swim" of the "Hub of the Universe."}}

